#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:463
msgid "**Properties**"
msgstr "**Eigenschappen**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:467
msgid ""
"If a property is listed here, its associated getter and setter methods must "
"also be renamed manually if used in the project. For example, PathFollow2D "
"and PathFollow3D's ``set_offset()`` and ``get_offset()`` must be renamed to "
"``set_progress()`` and ``get_progress()`` respectively."
msgstr ""
"Als een eigenschap hier genoemd wordt, moeten de getter- en settermethoden "
"die ermee zijn geassocieerd, ook handmatig worden genoemd als ze worden "
"gebruikt in het project. Bijvoorbeeld, ``set_offset()`` en ``get_offset()`` "
"van PathFollow2D en PathFollow3D moeten respectievelijk worden hernoemd naar "
"``set_progress()`` en ``get_progress()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:474
msgid "AudioServer's ``device`` is now ``output_device``."
msgstr "``device`` van AudioServer is nu ``output_device``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:475
msgid "BaseButton's ``group`` is now ``button_group``."
msgstr "``group`` van BaseButton is nu ``button_group``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:476
msgid "Camera3D's ``zfar`` is now ``far``."
msgstr "``zfar`` van Camera3D is nu ``far``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:477
msgid "Camera3D's ``znear`` is now ``near``"
msgstr "``znear`` van Camera3D is nu ``near``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:478
msgid "Control's ``margin`` is now ``offset``."
msgstr "``margin`` van Control is nu ``offset``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:479
msgid "InputEventMouseButton's ``doubleclick`` is now ``double_click``."
msgstr "``doubleclick`` van InputEventMouseButton is nu ``double_click``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:480
msgid "InputEventWithModifiers's ``alt`` is now ``alt_pressed``."
msgstr "``alt`` van InputEventWithModifiers is nu ``alt_pressed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:481
msgid "InputEventWithModifiers's ``command`` is now ``command_pressed``."
msgstr "``command`` van InputEventWithModifiers is nu ``command_pressed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:482
msgid "InputEventWithModifiers's ``control`` is now ``ctrl_pressed``."
msgstr "``control`` van InputEventWithModifiers is nu ``ctrl_pressed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:483
msgid "InputEventWithModifiers's ``meta`` is now ``meta_pressed``."
msgstr "``meta`` van InputEventWithModifiers is nu ``meta_pressed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:484
msgid "InputEventWithModifiers's ``shift`` is now ``shift_pressed``."
msgstr "``shift`` van InputEventWithModifiers is nu ``shift_pressed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:485
msgid "Label's ``percent_visible`` is now ``visible_ratio``."
msgstr "``percent_visible`` van Label is nu ``visible_ratio``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:486
msgid ""
"MultiPlayerAPI's ``refuse_new_network_connections`` is now "
"``refuse_new_connections``."
msgstr ""
"``refuse_new_network_connections`` van MultiPlayerAPI is nu "
"``refuse_new_connections``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:487
msgid "Node's ``filename`` is now ``scene_file_path``."
msgstr "``filename`` van Node is nu ``scene_file_path``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:488
msgid "PathFollow2D's ``rotate`` is now ``rotates``."
msgstr "``rotate`` van PathFollow2D is nu ``rotates``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:489
msgid "PathFollow2D and PathFollow3D's ``offset`` is now ``progress``."
msgstr "``offset`` van PathFollow2D en PathFollow3D is nu ``progress``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:490
msgid "RectangleShape2D's ``extents`` is now ``size``"
msgstr "``extents`` van RectangleShape2D is nu ``size``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:491
msgid "TextureProgressBar's ``percent_visible`` is now ``show_percentage``."
msgstr "``percent_visible`` van TextureProgressBar is nu ``show_percentage``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:492
msgid "Theme's ``off`` is now ``unchecked``."
msgstr "``off`` van Theme is nu ``unchecked``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:493
msgid "Theme's ``ofs`` is now ``offset``."
msgstr "``ofs`` van Theme is nu ``offset``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:494
msgid "Theme's ``on`` is now ``checked``."
msgstr "``on`` van Theme is nu ``checked``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:495
msgid "Window's ``window_title`` is now ``title``."
msgstr "``window_title`` van Window is nu ``title``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:496
msgid "WorldMarginShape2D's ``d`` is now ``distance``."
msgstr "``d`` van WorldMarginShape2D is nu ``distance``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:497
msgid ""
"The ``extents`` property on CSG nodes and VoxelGI will have to be replaced "
"with ``size``, with the set value halved (as they're no longer half-"
"extents). This also affects its setter/getter methods ``set_extents()`` and "
"``get_extents()``."
msgstr ""
"De eigenschap ``extents`` op CSG-knopen en VoxelGI moet worden vervangen "
"door ``size``, met de waarde gehalveerd (omdat het geen afstand vanaf het "
"midden meer is). Dit heeft ook effect op de setter-/gettermethoden "
"``set_extents()`` en ``get_extents()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:501
msgid ""
"The ``Engine.editor_hint`` property was removed in favor of the "
"``Engine.is_editor_hint()`` *method*. This is because it's read-only, and "
"properties in Godot are not used for read-only values."
msgstr ""
"De eigenschap ``Engine.editor_hint`` is verwijderd met als plaatsvervanger "
"de *methode* ``Engine.is_editor_hint()``. Dit is omdat het alleen-lezen is, "
"en eigenschappen in Godot niet worden gebruik voor alleen-lezenwaardes."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:507
msgid "**Enums**"
msgstr "**Enums**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:509
msgid "CPUParticles2D's ``FLAG_MAX`` is now ``PARTICLE_FLAG_MAX``."
msgstr "``FLAG_MAX`` van CPUParticles2D is nu ``PARTICLE_FLAG_MAX``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:511
msgid "**Signals**"
msgstr "**Signalen**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:513
msgid "FileSystemDock's ``instantiate`` is now ``instance``."
msgstr "``instantiate`` van FileSystemDock is nu ``instance``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:514
msgid ""
"CanvasItem's ``hide`` is now ``hidden``. This rename does **not** apply to "
"the ``hide()`` method, only the signal."
msgstr ""
"``hide`` van CanvasItem is nu ``hidden``. Deze hernoeming is **niet** van "
"toepassing op de methode ``hide()``, alleen op het signaal."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:516
msgid "Tween's ``tween_all_completed`` is now ``loop_finished``."
msgstr "``tween_all_completed`` van Tween is nu ``loop_finished``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:517
msgid "EditorSettings' ``changed`` is now ``settings_changed``."
msgstr "``changed`` van EditorSettings is nu ``settings_changed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:519
msgid "**Constants**"
msgstr "**Constanten**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:521
msgid ""
"Color names are now uppercase and use underscores between words. For "
"example, ``Color.palegreen`` is now ``Color.PALE_GREEN``."
msgstr ""
"Kleurennamen zijn nu in hoofdletters en gebruiken lage streepjes tussen "
"woorden. Bijvoorbeeld, ``Color.palegreen`` is nu ``Color.PALE_GREEN``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:523
msgid ""
"MainLoop's ``NOTIFICATION_`` constants were duplicated to ``Node`` which "
"means you can remove the ``MainLoop.`` prefix when referencing them."
msgstr ""
"``NOTIFICATION_``-constanten van MainLoop zijn gedupliceerd naar ``Node``, "
"wat betekent dat je het ``MainLoop.``-voorvoegsel kunt verwijderen als je "
"ernaar refereert."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:525
msgid ""
"MainLoop's ``NOTIFICATION_WM_QUIT_REQUEST`` is now "
"``NOTIFICATION_WM_CLOSE_REQUEST``."
msgstr ""
"``NOTIFICATION_WM_QUIT_REQUEST`` van MainLoop is nu "
"``NOTIFICATION_WM_CLOSE_REQUEST``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:528
msgid "Checking project settings"
msgstr "Controleren van project instellingen"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:530
msgid ""
"Several project settings were renamed, and some of them had their enums "
"changed in incompatible ways (such as shadow filter quality). This means you "
"may need to set some project settings' values again. Make sure the "
"**Advanced** toggle is enabled in the project settings dialog so you can see "
"all project settings."
msgstr ""
"Verschillende projectinstellingen zijn hernoemd en voor sommige zijn de "
"enums veranderd op incompatibele wijze (zoals schaduwfilterkwaliteit). Dit "
"betekent dat je misschien de waarden van sommige projectinstellingen opnieuw "
"moet instellen. Zorg ervoor dat de schakel **Geavanceerd** is ingeschakeld "
"in het projectinstellingenvenster, zodat je alle projectinstellingen kunt "
"zien."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:536
msgid "Checking Environment settings"
msgstr "Controleren van Environment-instellingen"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:538
msgid ""
"Graphics quality settings were moved from Environment properties to project "
"settings. This was done to make runtime quality adjustments easier, without "
"having to access the currently active Environment resource then modify its "
"properties."
msgstr ""
"Instellingen voor graphicskwaliteit zijn verplaatst van Environment-"
"eigenschappen naar projectinstellingen. Dit was om runtime-aanpassingen aan "
"de kwaliteit makkelijker te maken, zonder dat je eerst de actieve "
"Environment-bron moet ophalen en dan de eigenschappen moet aanpassen."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:543
msgid ""
"As a result, you will have to configure Environment quality settings in the "
"project settings as old Environment quality settings aren't converted "
"automatically to project settings."
msgstr ""
"Hierdoor moet je de Environment-kwaliteitsinstellingen handmatig "
"configureren in de projectinstellingen, omdat oude Environment-"
"kwaliteitsinstellingen niet automatisch worden geconverteerd naar "
"projectinstellingen."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:547
msgid ""
"If you have a graphics settings menu that changed environment properties in "
"Godot 3.x, you will have to change its code to "
"call :ref:`class_RenderingServer` methods that affect environment effects' "
"quality. Only the \"base\" toggle of each environment effect and its visual "
"knobs remain within the Environment resource."
msgstr ""
"Als je een graphics-instellingenmenu hebt dat omgevingseigenschappen "
"aanpaste in Godot 3.x, moet je de code ervan aanpassen "
"om :ref:`class_RenderingServer`-methoden aan te roepen die de kwaliteit van "
"omgevingseffecten bepalen. Alleen de \"basis\"-schakel van elk "
"omgevingseffect en de visuele regelaars ervan staan nog binnen de "
"Environment-bron."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:553
msgid "Updating shaders"
msgstr "Shaders bijwerken"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:555
msgid ""
"There have been some changes to shaders that aren't covered by the upgrade "
"tool. You will need to make some manual changes, especially if your shader "
"uses coordinate space transformations or a custom ``light()`` function."
msgstr ""
"Er zijn een paar wijzigingen aan shaders die niet worden afgevangen door de "
"upgrade-tool. Je moet enkele aanpassingen met de hand doen, vooral als je "
"shader gebruik maakt van transformaties op de coördinatenruimte, of een "
"aangepaste ``light()``-functie."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:559
msgid ""
"The ``.shader`` file extension is no longer supported, which means you must "
"rename ``.shader`` files to ``.gdshader`` and update references accordingly "
"in scene/resource files using an external text editor."
msgstr ""
"De bestandsextensie ``.shader`` wordt niet langer ondersteund, wat betekent "
"dat je ``.shader``-bestanden moet hernoemen naar ``.gdshader`` en "
"referenties waar nodig moet bijwerken in scène-/bronbestanden met een "
"externe teksteditor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:563
msgid "Some notable changes you will need to perform in shaders are:"
msgstr ""
"Enkele belangrijke veranderingen die je moet uitvoeren in shaders zijn:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:565
msgid ""
"Texture filter and repeat modes are now set on individual uniforms, rather "
"than the texture files themselves."
msgstr ""
"Texturefilter- en -herhaalmodi worden nu ingesteld op individuele uniforms, "
"in plaats van op de texturebestanden zelf."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:567
msgid "``hint_albedo`` is now ``source_color``."
msgstr "``hint_albedo`` is nu ``source_color``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:568
msgid "``hint_color`` is now ``source_color``."
msgstr "``hint_color`` is nu ``source_color``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:569
msgid ":ref:`Built in matrix variables were renamed. <doc_spatial_shader>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Ingebouwde matrix variabelen zijn hernoemd. <doc_spatial_shader>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:570
msgid ""
"Particles shaders no longer use the ``vertex()`` processor function. Instead "
"they use ``start()`` and ``process()``."
msgstr ""
"Partikelshaders gebruiken niet meer de ``vertex()``-processorfunctie. In "
"plaats daarvan gebruiken ze ``start()`` en ``process()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:572
msgid ""
"In the Forward+ and Mobile renderers, normalized device coordinates now have "
"a Z-range of ``[0.0,1.0]`` instead of ``[-1.0,1.0]``. When reconstructing "
"NDC from ``SCREEN_UV`` and depth, use ``vec3 ndc = vec3(SCREEN_UV * 2.0 - "
"1.0, depth);`` instead of ``vec3 ndc = vec3(SCREEN_UV, depth) * 2.0 - "
"1.0;``. The Compatibility renderer is unchanged, using the same NDC Z-range "
"as 3.x."
msgstr ""
"In de Forward+- en Mobile-renderers hebben genormaliseerde "
"toestelcoordinaten nu een Z-bereik van ``[0.0, 1.0]``, in plaats van "
"``[-1.0,1.0]``. Gebruik bij het reconstrueren van NDC uit ``SCREEN_UV`` en "
"diepte nu ``vec3 ndc = vec3(SCREEN_UV * 2.0 - 1.0, depth);`` in plaats van "
"``vec3 ndc = vec3(SCREEN_UV, depth) * 2.0 - 1.0;``. Voor Compatibility-"
"renderer is niets veranderd; deze gebruikt hetzelfdeZ-bereik voor NDC als in "
"3.x."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:577
msgid ""
"The lighting model changed. If your shader has a custom ``light()`` "
"function, you may need to make changes to get the same visual result."
msgstr ""
"De belichtingsmodel is veranderd. Als je shader een eigen ``light()`` "
"functie heeft, moet je deze misschien aanpassen om hetzelfde visuele "
"resultaat te krijgen."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:579
msgid ""
"In 4.3 and up, the reverse Z depth buffer technique is now implemented, "
"which may break advanced shaders. See `Introducing Reverse Z (AKA I'm sorry "
"for breaking your shader) <https://godotengine.org/article/introducing-"
"reverse-z/>`__."
msgstr ""
"In 4.3 en hoger is nu de omgekeerde Z-dieptebuffertechniek geïmplementeerd, "
"wat geavanceerde shaders kan breken. Zie `Introducing Reverse Z (AKA I'm "
"sorry for breaking your shader) <https://godotengine.org/article/introducing-"
"reverse-z/>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:583
msgid "See :ref:`doc_shading_language` for more information."
msgstr "Bekijk :ref:`doc_shading_language` voor verdere informatie."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:585
msgid ""
"This list is not exhaustive. If you made all the changes mentioned here and "
"your shader still doesn't work, try asking for help in one of the `community "
"channels <https://godotengine.org/community/>`__."
msgstr ""
"Dit is geen volledige lijst. Als je alle veranderingen die hier zijn "
"genoemd, hebt gemaakt en je shader werkt nog steeds niet, probeer dan om om "
"hulp te vragen in een van de `community channels <https://godotengine.org/"
"community/>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:589
msgid "Updating scripts to take backwards-incompatible changes into account"
msgstr "Scripts updaten met het oog op terugwaarts-incompatibele veranderingen"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:591
msgid ""
"Some changes performed between Godot 3.x and 4 are not renames, but they "
"still break backwards compatibility due to different default behavior."
msgstr ""
"Sommige veranderingen die zijn uitgevoerd tussen Godot 3.x en 4 zijn geen "
"hernoemingen, maar breken wel terugwaartse compatibiliteit vanwege ander "
"standaardgedrag."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:594
msgid "The most notable examples of this are:"
msgstr "De belangrijkste voorbeelden hiervan zijn:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:596
msgid ""
"Lifecycle functions such as ``_ready()`` and ``_process()`` no longer "
"implicitly call parent classes' functions that have the same name. Instead, "
"you must use ``super()`` at the top of a lifecycle function in the child "
"class so that the parent class function is called first."
msgstr ""
"Levenscyclusfuncties zoals ``_ready()`` en ``_process()`` roepen niet meer "
"impliciet de functies van alle ouderklassen aan die dezelfde naam dragen. In "
"plaats daarvan moet je ``super()`` gebruiken bovenaan een "
"levenscyclusfunctie in de kindklasse, zodat de functie in de ouderklasse "
"eerst wordt aangeroepen."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:600
msgid ""
"Both :ref:`class_String` and :ref:`class_StringName` are now exposed to "
"GDScript. This allows for greater optimization, as StringName is "
"specifically designed to be used for \"constant\" strings that are created "
"once and reused many times. These types are not strictly equivalent to each "
"other, which means ``is_same(\"example\", &\"example\")`` returns ``false``. "
"Although in most cases they are interchangeable (``\"example\" == "
"&\"example\"`` returns ``true``), sometimes you may have to replace "
"``\"example\"`` with ``&\"example\"``."
msgstr ""
"Zowel :ref:`class_String` en :ref:`class_StringName` zijn nu beschikbaar in "
"GDScript. Hiermee is betere optimalisatie mogelijk, want StringName is "
"specifiek ontworpen om te worden gebruikt voor \"constante\" strings, die "
"één keer worden aangemaakt en vele malen worden hergebruikt. Deze types zijn "
"niet strikt genomen aan elkaar equivalent, wat betekent dat "
"``is_same(\"example\", &\"example\")`` ``false`` teruggeeft. Hoewel ze in de "
"meeste gevallen inwisselbaar zijn (``\"example\" == &\"example\"`` geeft "
"``true`` terug), moet je soms misschien ``\"example\"`` vervangen door "
"``&\"example\"``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:607
msgid ""
":ref:`GDScript setter and getter syntax "
"<doc_gdscript_basics_setters_getters>` was changed, but it's only partially "
"converted by the conversion tool. In most cases, manual changes are required "
"to make setters and getters working again."
msgstr ""
":ref:`De setter- and gettersyntax van GDScript "
"<doc_gdscript_basics_setters_getters>` is veranderd, en wordt maar deels "
"geconverteerd door de conversietool. In de meeste gevallen zijn handmatige "
"aanpassingen nodig om setters en getters weer te laten werken."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:610
msgid ""
":ref:`GDScript signal connection syntax <doc_gdscript_signals>` was changed. "
"The conversion tool will use the string-based syntax which is still present "
"in Godot 4, but it's recommended to switch to the :ref:`class_Signal`-based "
"syntax described on the linked page. This way, strings are no longer "
"involved, which avoids issues with signal name errors that can only be "
"discovered at runtime."
msgstr ""
":ref:`De syntax voor signaalkoppeling in GDScript <doc_gdscript_signals>` is "
"veranderd. De conversietool gebruikt de op strings gebaseerde syntax die nog "
"wel aanwezig is in Godot 4, maar het is aangeraden om over te schakelen naar "
"de syntax gebaseerd op :ref:`class_Signal`, beschreven op de gelinkte "
"pagina. Op deze manier worden er geen strings meer gebruikt; dit voorkomt "
"problemen met fouten in signaalnamen die alleen kunnen worden ondekt tijdens "
"runtime."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:615
msgid ""
"Built-in scripts that are :ref:`tool scripts "
"<doc_running_code_in_the_editor>` do not get the ``tool`` keyword converted "
"to the ``@tool`` annotation."
msgstr ""
"Voor ingebouwde scripts die :ref:`toolscripts "
"<doc_running_code_in_the_editor>` zijn, wordt het ``tool``-sleutelwoord niet "
"geconverteerd naar de ``@tool``-annotatie."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:617
msgid ""
"The Tween node was removed in favor of Tweeners, which are also available in "
"Godot 3.5 and later. See the `original pull request <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot/pull/41794>`__ for details."
msgstr ""
"De Tween-knoop is verwijderd en vervangen door Tweeners, die ook beschikbaar "
"zijn in Godot 3.5 en later. Zie het `originele pull request <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/41794>`__ voor details."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:621
msgid ""
"``randomize()`` is now automatically called on project load, so "
"deterministic randomness with the global RandomNumberGenerator instance "
"requires manually setting a seed in a script's ``_ready()`` function."
msgstr ""
"``randomize()`` wordt nu automatisch aangeroepen bij het inladen van het "
"project, dus voor deterministische willekeurigheid met de globable "
"RandomNumberGenerator-instantie moet handmatig een seed worden ingesteld in "
"de ``_ready()``-functie van een script."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:624
msgid ""
"``call_group()``, ``set_group()`` and ``notify_group()`` are now immediate "
"by default. If calling an expensive function, this may result in stuttering "
"when used on a group containing a large number of nodes. To use deferred "
"calls like before, replace ``call_group(...)`` with "
"``call_group_flags(SceneTree.GROUP_CALL_DEFERRED, ...)`` (and do the same "
"with ``set_group()`` and ``notify_group()`` respectively)."
msgstr ""
"``call_group()``, ``set_group()`` en ``notify_group()`` zijn worden nu "
"standaard onmiddellijk uitgevoerd. Als je een dure functie aanroept, kan dit "
"zorgen voor haperen, als het wordt gebruikt op een groep met een groot "
"aantal knopen. Om uitgestelde aanroepen te gebruiken zoals voorheen, kun je "
"``call_group(...)`` vervangen door "
"``call_group_flags(SceneTree.GROUP_CALL_DEFERRED, ...)`` (en hetzelfde met "
"``set_group()`` en ``notify_group()``, respectievelijk)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:630
msgid ""
"Instead of ``rotation_degrees``, the ``rotation`` property is exposed to the "
"editor, which is automatically displayed as degrees in the Inspector dock. "
"This may break animations, as the conversion is not handled automatically by "
"the conversion tool."
msgstr ""
"In plaats van ``rotation_degrees`` is nu de eigenschap ``rotation`` "
"beschikbaar in de editor, en wordt deze automatisch getoond in graden in het "
"Infopaneel. Dit kan animaties kapotmaken, omdat de conversie niet "
"automatisch wordt doorgevoerd door de conversietool."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:634
msgid ""
":ref:`class_AABB`'s ``has_no_surface()`` was inverted and renamed to "
"``has_surface()``."
msgstr ""
"``has_no_surface()`` uit :ref:`class_AABB` is omgekeerd en hernoemd naar "
"``has_surface()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:635
msgid ""
":ref:`class_AABB` and :ref:`class_Rect2`'s ``has_no_area()`` was inverted "
"and renamed to ``has_area()``."
msgstr ""
"``has_no_area()`` uit :ref:`class_AABB` en :ref:`class_Rect2` is omgekeerd "
"en hernoemd naar ``has_area()``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:637
msgid ""
":ref:`class_AnimatedTexture`'s ``fps`` property was replaced by "
"``speed_scale``, which works the same as AnimationPlayer's "
"``playback_speed`` property."
msgstr ""
"De ``fps``-eigenschap uit :ref:`class_AnimatedTexture` is vervangen door "
"``speed_scale``, die hetzelfde werkt als de eigenschap ``playback_speed`` "
"uit de AnimationPlayer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:639
msgid ""
":ref:`class_AnimatedSprite2D` and :ref:`class_AnimatedSprite3D` now allow "
"negative ``speed_scale`` values. This may break animations if you relied on "
"``speed_scale`` being internally clamped to ``0.0``."
msgstr ""
":ref:`class_AnimatedSprite2D` en :ref:`class_AnimatedSprite3D` laten nu "
"negatieve ``speed_scale``-waarden toe. Dit kan animaties kapotmaken als je "
"ervan uitging dat ``speed_scale`` intern werd afgekapt bij ``0.0``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:642
msgid ""
":ref:`class_AnimatedSprite2D` and :ref:`class_AnimatedSprite3D`'s "
"``playing`` property was removed. Use ``play()``/``stop()`` method instead "
"OR configure ``autoplay`` animation via the SpriteFrames bottom panel (but "
"not both at once)."
msgstr ""
"De eigenschap ``playing`` uit :ref:`class_AnimatedSprite2D` "
"en :ref:`class_AnimatedSprite3D` is verwijderd. Gebruik in plaats daarvan de "
"methode ``play()``/``stop()`` OF configureer de ``autoplay``-animatie in het "
"SpriteFrames-paneel onderaan (maar niet allebei tegelijk)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:645
msgid ""
":ref:`class_Array`'s ``slice()`` second parameter (``end``) is now "
"*exclusive*, instead of being inclusive. For example, this means that ``[1, "
"2, 3].slice(0, 1)`` now returns ``[1]`` instead of ``[1, 2]``."
msgstr ""
"De tweede parameter van ``slice()`` uit :ref:`class_Array` (``end``) is nu "
"*exclusief*, in plaats van inclusief. Dit betekent bijvoorbeeld dat ``[1, 2, "
"3].slice(0, 1)`` nu ``[1]`` teruggeeft in plaats van ``[1, 2]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:648
msgid ""
":ref:`class_BaseButton`'s signals are now ``button_up`` and ``button_down``. "
"The ``pressed`` property is now ``button_pressed``."
msgstr ""
"De signalen van :ref:`class_BaseButton` zijn nu ``button_up`` en "
"``button_down``. De eigenschap ``pressed`` heet nu ``button_pressed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:650
msgid ""
":ref:`class_Camera2D`'s ``rotating`` property was replaced by "
"``ignore_rotation``, which has inverted behavior."
msgstr ""
"De eigenschap ``rotating`` van :ref:`class_Camera2D` is vervangen door "
"``ignore_rotation``, wat omgekeerd gedrag heeft."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:652
msgid ""
"Camera2D's ``zoom`` property was inverted: higher values are now more zoomed "
"in, instead of less."
msgstr ""
"De eigenschap ``zoom`` van Camera2D is omgekeerd: hogere waarden zijn nu "
"verder ingezoomd, in plaats van minder ver."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:654
msgid ""
":ref:`class_Node`'s ``remove_and_skip()`` method was removed. If you need to "
"reimplement it in a script, you can use the `old C++ implementation <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/7936b3cc4c657e4b273b376068f095e1e0e4d82a/"
"scene/main/node.cpp#L1910-L1945>`__ as a reference."
msgstr ""
"De methode ``remove_and_skip()`` van :ref:`class_Node` is verwijderd. Als je "
"het moet herimplementeren in een script, kun je de `oude C++-implementatie "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/"
"7936b3cc4c657e4b273b376068f095e1e0e4d82a/scene/main/node.cpp#L1910-L1945>`__ "
"gebruiken ter referentie."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:658
msgid ""
"``OS.get_system_time_secs()`` should be converted to "
"``Time.get_time_dict_from_system()[\"second\"]``."
msgstr ""
"``OS.get_system_time_secs()`` moet worden geconverteerd naar "
"``Time.get_time_dict_from_system()[\"second\"]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:660
msgid ""
":ref:`class_ResourceSaver`'s ``save()`` method now has its arguments swapped "
"around (``resource: Resource, path: String``). This also applies "
"to :ref:`class_ResourceFormatSaver`'s ``_save()`` method."
msgstr ""
"Voor de methode ``save()`` van :ref:`class_ResourceSaver` zijn de argumenten "
"nu omgewisseld (``resource: Resource, path: String``). Dit geldt ook voor de "
"methode ``_save()`` van :ref:`class_ResourceFormatSaver`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:663
msgid ""
"A :ref:`class_StreamPeerTCP` must have ``poll()`` called on it to update its "
"state, instead of relying on ``get_status()`` automatically polling: "
"`GH-59582 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/59582>`__"
msgstr ""
"Voor een :ref:`class_StreamPeerTCP` moet ``poll()`` aangeroepen worden "
"voordat het zijn toestand bijwerkt, in plaats van dat je ervan uit kunt gaan "
"dat ``get_status()`` automatisch pollt: `GH-59582 <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot/pull/59582>`__"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:666
msgid ""
":ref:`class_String`'s ``right()`` method `has changed behavior <https://"
"github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/36180>`__: it now returns a number of "
"characters from the right of the string, rather than the right side of the "
"string from a given position. If you need the old behavior, you can use "
"``substr()`` instead."
msgstr ""
"De methode ``right()`` van :ref:`class_String` `heeft veranderd gedrag "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/36180>`__: het geeft nu een "
"aantal tekens vanaf de rechterkant van de string terug, in plaats van de "
"rechterkant van de string vanaf een bepaalde positie. Als je het oude gedrag "
"nodig hebt, kun je in plaats daarvan ``substr()`` gebruiken."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:670
msgid ""
"``is_connected_to_host()`` was removed from StreamPeerTCP and PacketPeerUDP "
"as per `GH-59582 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/59582>`__. "
"``get_status()`` can be used in StreamPeerTCP instead. "
"``is_socket_connected()`` can be used in :ref:`class_PacketPeerUDP` instead."
msgstr ""
"``is_connected_to_host()`` is verwijderd van StreamPeerTCP en PacketPeerUDP; "
"zie `GH-59582 <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/59582>`__. "
"``get_status()`` kan in StreamPeerTCP worden gebruikt ter vervanging. "
"``is_socket_connected()`` kan in :ref:`class_PacketPeerUDP` worden gebruikt "
"ter vervanging."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:674
msgid ""
"In ``_get_property_list()``, the ``or_lesser`` property hint string is now "
"``or_less``."
msgstr ""
"In ``_get_property_list()`` heet de eigenschapshintstring ``or_lesser`` nu "
"``or_less``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:675
msgid ""
"In ``_get_property_list()``, the ``noslider`` property hint string is now "
"``no_slider``."
msgstr ""
"In ``_get_property_list()`` heet de eigenschapshintstring ``noslider`` nu "
"``no_slider``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.rst:676
msgid ""
"VisualShaderNodeVec4Parameter now takes a :ref:`class_Vector4` as parameter "
"instead of a :ref:`class_Quaternion`."
msgstr ""
"VisualShaderNodeVec4Parameter neemt nu een :ref:`class_Vector4` als "
"parameter in plaats van een :ref:`class_Quaternion`."

