#: ../../docs/tutorials/animation/animation_tree.rst:373
msgid ""
"By default, blending happens in the *Continuous* mode, by interpolating "
"points inside the closest triangle in ``BlendSpace2D``, or in the line "
"between points in ``BlendSpace1D``. However, this may not always be the best "
"choice. For instance, when dealing with frame-by-frame 2D animations, you "
"may want to switch to the *Discrete* mode, in which the intermediate states "
"of the blend do not appear in the result. Alternatively, if you want to "
"retain the current play position when switching between discrete animations, "
"the *Carry* mode allows you to do so. These modes can be set with the "
"*Blend* menu."
